course: dictionary
lesson: 11137
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists each meaning with a number, so you have to choose the right one. The context, meaning the words and sentences around the word, tells you which meaning is meant. «Ruth was a young widow from Moab.» Here a widow is a woman whose husband has died.
explain: The same word can mean something very different in another sentence. «The black widow has a dangerous bite.» Here widow is the name of a kind of spider. The word black and the word bite are your clues that this is not about a woman.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have chosen well. Words can also change their form: a man whose wife has died is a widower, and a person who has lost a husband or wife has been widowed.
fact: «Widow» has two main meanings: a woman whose husband has died and who has not married again, or, in printing, a single short line left alone at the top of a page or column.
fact: «Widower» means a man whose wife has died.
fact: «Widowed» means having lost your husband or wife through death, as in «was widowed».
fact: «Black widow» is a kind of spider, found in North America and Australia, whose bite is dangerous.
fact: The redback spider is a relative of the black widow, and it hides in dry, sheltered places.
exercise: «Ruth was a young widow from Moab.» What is a widow in this sentence? | A spider that lives in dry places | A girl who has moved to a new country | *A woman whose husband has died | A man who lives alone
exercise: «The black widow has a dangerous bite.» In this sentence, what does widow mean? | A short line at the top of a page | *A kind of spider | A woman who has lost her husband | A brave, poor character in a story
exercise: What do we call a man whose wife has died? | *A widower | A widow | A printer | A redback
test: Which word means a man whose wife has died? | *Widower | Widen | Widow | Window
test: «The kind neighbours helped the widow with her shopping.» What does widow mean? | *A woman whose husband has died | A short line left alone at the top of a page | A kind of spider | A word that means very old
exam: In printing, what is a widow? | *A single short line left alone at the top of a page or column | A word that means very old | A woman whose husband has died | A kind of spider
